#### Surviving Adaptive Mechanism: Class-Group 2D-CRT Capacity Constructor (CG-2D-CRT)

(1) Description. Fix beta in (0, 1/3) (concretely beta = 1/4), smoothness bound B = L_N[beta, kappa], and box side K = L_N[1 - beta, nu] with nu = (1 - beta)/(4*kappa) + eps. Sample pi(B) + O(log N) independent reduced positive-definite binary quadratic forms Q_m(k, v) = A_m k^2 + B_m k v + C_m v^2 of discriminant -4N representing known factor-base walks in Cl(-4N) (so A_m, C_m ~ sqrt(N)). Precompute the mod-q^(e_q) residue syndrome of (A_m, B_m, C_m) for all primes q <= B in L_N[beta, kappa] bit operations (notes/sinonobliv_results.md:141-150). Query an algebraic beyond-Johnson 2D-CRT list decoder on (k, v) in [1, K]^2 to output one pair with valuation agreement sum_{q^e | Q_m(k,v)} ln q >= ln Q_m(k, v), reading off Q_m(k, v)'s prime factorization from the agreeing coordinates. Each hit yields a certified Cl(-4N) relation with NO second residue side to test; GF(2) elimination yields a 2-torsion ambiguous form splitting N = p*q with probability >= 1/2.

(2) Exponent ledger (x = log N, F_alpha = x^alpha (log x)^(1 - alpha), beta = 1/4):
- Candidate norm size: Q_m(k, v) <= 3*sqrt(N)*K^2, so log X = (1/2 + o(1))*x.
- Smoothness bound: B = L_N[1/4, kappa], log B = kappa * x^(1/4) * (log x)^(3/4).
- Dickman parameter: u_0 = log X / log B = (1/(2*kappa)) * x^(3/4) * (log x)^(-3/4), giving -log rho(u_0) = (3/(8*kappa) + o(1)) * F_{3/4}.
- Box size: K = exp(((3/(16*kappa)) + eps) * F_{3/4}), so [1, K]^2 holds K^2 * rho(u_0) = exp(2*eps * F_{3/4}) >> 1 witnesses on average; as eps -> 0, mean list size per form is O(1).
- Relations and cost: pi(B) = L_N[1/4, kappa] relations; if one 2D-CRT decode costs pi(B)^a = L_N[1/4, a*kappa] and sparse LA costs pi(B)^2, total time is L_N[1/4, max((1+a)*kappa, 2*kappa)], giving alpha = 1/4 < 1/3 for any fixed polynomial decoder exponent a >= 1.

(3) Barrier evasion and why it is not the four barred classes in disguise:
- Prop SI single-interval cap (notes/suffmap_results.md:337-338): 1D intervals [kN, kN+h] leave an unfactored residue v = u - kN <= L[1 - beta] whose smoothness test costs L[1 - 2*beta], forcing max(beta, 1 - 2*beta) >= 1/3. CG-2D-CRT has NO second side: Q_m(k, v) is an ideal norm in Q(sqrt(-N)).
- smoothbuild Theorem SS (notes/smoothbuild_results.md:26-28, 146-152): applies only when an unconditioned side is tested at Dickman rate; here the certificate is built jointly with (k, v).
- sihard Theorem J (notes/sihard_results.md:408-440): bounds only Johnson-radius certificates where agreement >= sqrt(ln(K^2) * ln P) ~ sqrt(F_{3/4} * x * L[1/4]) >> x. Here required agreement is (1/2)*x while message entropy is ln(K^2) ~ F_{3/4} = o(x); agreement/entropy ~ (4*kappa/3)*(x/log x)^(1/4) -> infinity, sitting strictly above counting capacity yet below Johnson.
- siconstruct Prop CV (notes/siconstruct_results.md:111-164): embeds one interval into R^(pi(B)+1); K^2 quadratic values Q_m(k, v) form L[3/4] disconnected targets in Adleman's real log-lattice, whereas mod q^(e_q) they form one degree-2 algebraic code over prod_{q<=B} Z/q^(e_q)Z.
- navigate Theorem DLB / suffmap Prop DLT (notes/navigate_results.md:196-232; notes/suffmap_results.md:473-484): by contrast, we note that a linear-form 2D-Bohr-CRT decoder on {k*N + v : k <= L[1-beta], |v| <= B} WOULD also decode k*p + t*v (since |t*v| < B*p << K*p keeps log u ~ log p), solving F_p^* DL in L_p[beta] without ECM booting. Restricting to positive-definite forms of discriminant -4N < 0 (where half the primes are inert and Cl(-4p) has trivial genus) blocks that reduction (notes/sihard_results.md:231-238).

(4) Single assumption (speculative): existence of a poly(pi(B))-time list decoder for positive-definite binary-quadratic CRT codes at vanishing rate R ~ F_{1-beta}/(x*pi(B)) and agreement fraction ~ 1/(2*pi(B)).

(5) Cheapest falsification test: along the toy beta = 1/4 path for 48-to-96-bit N, run algebraic interpolation / belief-propagation / lattice-lift decoding on Q_m(k, v) mod q^(e_q) capped at pi(B)^2 operations and test whether empirical success probability decays slower than K^(-2). (Not run for beyond-Johnson algebra; E1 confirmed naive sub-threshold residue steering gives 0.60x-0.77x of random products at 32-48 bits, killing heuristic beam search.)

---

### 2. H5 (Sparse Selection from Boxes > B) and Cross-Family Composition

We establish four kills closing major pieces of H5 and smoothness-biased selection, leaving two narrow survivors.

- Kill K2a (Rank-2 H5 closed up to doubly-subexponential boxes — Farey-Trapezoid Lemma FT, proved): In notes/resbarrier_results.md:177-181, 226-235, Corollary RB2 needed H5 (E <= B/(16*(D+1))) because Davenport's error 2*(D+1)*(2*E+1) is linear in E. Partitioning primitive (a, b) in [-E, E]^2 (gcd(a, b) = 1, 0 < |F(a, b)| <= X, deg F = D >= 3, disc F != 0) by nearest root theta_i and dyadic shells b in [2^m, 2^(m+1)): consecutive primitive ratios satisfy a_{r+1}/b_{r+1} - a_r/b_r >= 1/(b_r*b_{r+1}) > 2^(-2m-2), so s - 1 <= 2^(2m+2)*delta. By convexity and triangle inequality on C, every point in the trapezoid {(t*y, y) : y in [2^(m-1), 2^m], t in [a_1/b_1, a_s/b_s]} (disjoint across m, area (3/8)*2^(2m)*delta) satisfies |F(t*y, y)| <= 3^(D-1)*X. Summing over m and two charts proves:
  #{primitive (a, b) in [-E, E]^2 : 0 < |F(a, b)| <= X} <= 384 * D * 9^((D-1)/D) * A_F * X^(2/D) + 4 * D * (floor(log_2 E) + 2).
  This removes H5 at rank 2 for all boxes up to E <= 2^(B/(16*D)) = exp(Omega(L_N[beta]/x^(1/3))), covering all polynomial, N^(O(1)), and L_N[gamma] boxes (gamma < 1). Pre-registered check E2 (12 GNFS/SNFS/skewed forms, D in {4,5}, E = 256, 667 thresholds): 0/667 violations; cusp count 2 <= FT error 160-200 vs Davenport's 10260-12312 (>61x tighter).

- Kill K2b (Smoothness-concentrating polynomial selectors inside large boxes, killed): To beat Dickman rho(u) at fixed size X via algebraic splitting (notes/sinonobliv_results.md:210-218), let (a(u, v), b(u, v)) be coprime degree-e forms mapping [-U, U]^2 into [-U^e, U^e]^2. In K[u, v] (K = Q[X]/(f), deg d), a(u, v) - alpha*b(u, v) has degree e, so F(a(u, v), b(u, v)) = N_{K/Q}(a - alpha*b) splits into at most k <= e irreducible factors over Q[u, v]. Dividing log|F_1| ~ x/d + d*e*log U into k <= e pieces leaves k * u_piece = u_total, saving only log e inside log u (L^(o(1))) unless u_piece = O(1); but u_piece = O(1) requires d*log U <= O(log B) <= O(log U), forcing d = O(1) and rational norm |a - m*b| >= N^(1/d) = N^(Omega(1)) -> L[1/2]. Similarly, 1D shift-compositions Q(t) = f(m + P(t)) with f(m) = N = p*q satisfy prod_s |R_s(c_j)| = p*q at every root c_j of P, forcing >= M - 2 factors to be +-1 (or exposing gcd(R_s(c_j), N) in {p, q}).

- Kill K2c (Rank-r >= 3 curve pullbacks and archimedean tubes, killed): Any degree-m curve selector psi : Z^2 -> [-E, E]^r intersects the mod-p linking hyperplane in P^(r-1)(F_p_bar) by Bezout, forcing N^(2m) | disc(F o psi) and reducing to rank-2 Lemma FT (alpha >= 1/3). Continuous LLL tubes steering k < r real linear forms to width eta in [-E, E]^r have volume ~ E^(r-k)*eta^k = e^C, forcing |F| >= floor * e^C * E^(D-r), strictly worse than E = e^(C/r) since D > r.

- Kill K2d (Codex's non-subfield frame-less Door (ii) family closed): notes/grdeg_results.md:71-72, 188-189 left (1, s, t, t^2) vs (1, s', t, t^2) (K_0 = Q(t) cubic, [K:K_0] = 2) open because rank 4 has no O_{K_0}-module action. However, Proposition RR1-RR2 (notes/grdeg_results.md:133-145) needs NO module action — only that phi|_{K_0} = phi'|_{K_0} agree and s, s' share a root mod N over O_{K_0}. Hence N | Norm_{K_0/Q}(Res_{K_0}(f, g)), forcing h(s) + h(s') >= (d_0/d)*x = x/2 (L[1/2] floor) whenever a_2 != 0, while a_2 = 0 gives W = W'. Confirmed in pre-registered E3 across 9 LLL-built instances (21-42 bits): 9/9 have N | Norm(Res), W = W' at a_2 = 0, and min_{a_2!=0} log|F|/log N in [1.47, 2.12].

#### Surviving Mechanism M1: Type-D Relative-Rank m >= 3 Non-Power Linked Module (grdeg Door (i))
(1) Description. Over a fixed quadratic field k = Q(sqrt(d_0)) ([k:Q] = e = 2) splitting mod N with a known/extracted root s_0 of mu_k mod N, build degree-n extensions K, K' over k (d = 2n, D = 4n) sharing an O_k-module of relative rank m >= 3 (total Z-rank r = 2m) with non-power generators linked mod (N, theta_k - s_0), sampling a in {0, +-1}^r.
(2) Ledger: d ~ sqrt(x/log x), m ~ x^(1/4)*(log x)^(3/4), r = 2m, C = r*ln 3 ~ F_{1/4}. If generator heights stay at e*x/d (c = 0), log X ~ e*x/d + 2*d*ln x ~ sqrt(x*log x), B = L_N[1/4], u ~ x^(1/4), giving alpha = 1/4.
(3) Barrier evasion: Delta_F = 0 and 0 frames evade rank3 R1 (notes/rank3_results.md:126) and rankdegen FH (notes/rankdegen_results.md:232); a_j in {0, +-1} evades H5_r (notes/rank3_results.md:202); non-power m >= 3 evades grdeg Prop RR3 (notes/grdeg_results.md:146-152), while V_F = infinity (O_k^x action) blocks relative Bean-Thunder. Note SL0 (notes/grdeg_results.md:167-170) still requires root s_0 mod N.
(4) Single assumption (speculative): failure of both relative G_m and "relative R1" over O_k, plus cheap access to s_0 mod N.
(5) Cheapest falsification test: E3 tested pure-cubic m = 3 over Q(i) (21-42 bits), getting min log|F|/log N ~ 1.81-1.92 (pure cubics pay |d_i| ~ N^(1/2)). The sharp decisive test is LLL-searching general degree-n cubics/quartics over Z[i] with non-power m = 3 generators and checking if min_{A_2!=0} log|F|/log N drops toward 2/d as n = 3, 4, 5 grows or tracks 2*(m-1)/(2n-1).

#### Surviving Mechanism M3: Evaluated Multi-Presentation Split Pencils (nonexact O1/O2)
(1) Description. Across a pencil of presentations F_nu(X) with F_nu(m) == 0 (mod N) (m ~ N^(1/d)), select split polynomials P_A(X) = prod_{j=1}^M (X - a_j) (|a_j| <= B = L_N[beta], beta < 1/3) whose mod-(N, F_nu) evaluation satisfies P_A(m) == v_A (mod N) with 0 < |v_A| <= L_N[2*beta] via non-exact wraps P_A - F_nu*Q_A - r_A = N*T_A (T_A != 0).
(2) Ledger: Shifted factor base {m - a : |a| <= B} U {p <= B} of size L_N[beta]; M ~ x/log m, log|v_A| <= c*F_{2*beta} tested at B = L_N[beta] costs L_N[beta] per relation -> alpha = beta < 1/3 if per-member generation costs L_N[beta, O(1)].
(3) Barrier evasion: T_A != 0 evades ptebarrier Theorem W (notes/ptebarrier_results.md; notes/ptesplit_results.md:49-54); k = M + 1 growing pieces evade suffmap Theorem SS's k = O(1) clause (notes/suffmap_results.md:153-155); moving degree-M products evade rank-2 Cor RB2. (Single-presentation seeded PTE matching d - t symmetric functions is killed by Newton power-sum pigeonhole (d-t)^2/2 <= d => t ~ d => |v| ~ N.)
(4) Single assumption (speculative): an N-coherent algebraic generator producing non-exact pencil witnesses in L_N[beta] amortized time (beating nonexact Prop LIN's N^(1-o(1)) lattice enumeration, notes/nonexact_results.md:61-64).
(5) Cheapest falsification test: for 32-48-bit N and B = round(2^(n/5)), search 2-presentation pencils F_0 + nu*F_1 for split P_A of degree M = 6..10 with |P_A(m) mod* N| <= B^2 via algebraic resultant/Gröbner elimination; falsified if per-hit cost tracks brute-force (2B)^M * (B^2/N).

---

### 3. Literature Scan (2024–2026)

1. Zhang & Xuan (Oct 2026, arXiv:2610.28338), unconditional subexponential SLPs for factorial multiples tau(m*k!) <= exp(O((log k)^(2/3)*(log log k)^(1/3))): At k = floor(sqrt(N)), circuit size is L_N[2/3] >> L_N[1/3], and uncontrolled multiple m risks N | m (gcd = N). Blocked at L[1/3] by circuit size and notes/slpcirc_results.md:82-95 (Prop R).
2. Brakensiek et al. (Sept 2026, arXiv:2609.08005) & Jeronimo (Sept 2026, arXiv:2609.05870), plain Reed-Solomon list decoding to capacity: Require prime fields and runtime q^(eps^(-O(1))); at CRT smooth-reconstruction parameters, relative agreement ~ 1/pi(B) -> 0 blows the exponent above sieving, and Z/q^(e_q) lacks global Hasse derivations. Blocked by notes/crtdecode_results.md:263-274 and notes/pilist_results.md:352-363.
3. Mulder, Sterner & van Woerden (2025 / ANTS XVII 2026, arXiv:2509.17699 / ePrint 2025/1462), large smooth twins from short vectors in prime lattices: Operates in the dense unplanted SVP regime (dim <= 168); factoring targets ln(kN) require promise-CVP_{1+O(1/x)} in dim pi(B) = L[1/3], costing 2^(Theta(pi(B))). Blocked by notes/siconstruct_results.md:106-175 (Prop CV) and notes/schnorrcvp_results.md:62-64.
4. Tesoro et al. (arXiv:2410.16355, Phys. Rev. A), Al-Hasso & von der Leyen (Oct 2025, arXiv:2510.19390, p-bits), and VQE-Schnorr (arXiv:2411.16632): Physics heuristics on Schnorr's prime-lattice CVP up to <= 130 bits. At Schnorr's low dimensions, expected fac-relations are < 10^(-51) at 400 bits; valid dim >= (ln N)^(3/2) faces exponential energy barriers and |u*w| >= N - 1. Blocked by notes/schnorrcvp_results.md:39-44, 68-74 (Theorem R) and notes/resbarrier_results.md:388.
5. Huang et al. (2024–2026, arXiv:2409.08784), Double Index Calculus in F_p^*: Dual g^a and b^c systems colliding on one factor-base element — a wrong-model claim, as one shared prime with uneliminated cofactors leaves an underdetermined system (Lemma KI singleton barrier, notes/smoothbuild_results.md:187-194), and at best saves O(1) in L_p[1/2].
6. Le Gluher, Spaenlehauer & Thomé (2024–2025, Math. Cryptology) and Robinson (2024–2025, 4D orthotope TNFS): Le Gluher et al. show NFS's o(1) decays as (4/3)*log log log N / log log N (alpha = 1/3 unchanged); Robinson's 4D TNFS targets medium-char F_{p^n} where p-constraint < p^n. For Z/N, tower degree eta cancels or worsens height to 2*eta. Blocked by notes/heurnfs_results.md:342-380 (Barriers B2, B3) and notes/rank3_results.md:231-249 (Corollary R3).
7. Streaming/dequantized Regev studies (2024–2026, e.g. arXiv:2610.06733, Ekerå-Gärtner PQCrypto 2024): Classical lattice post-processing works only given quantum dual-lattice phase samples; classically, Shor/Regev state Schmidt rank equals multiplicative order r, so tensor/classical simulation costs Theta(r). Blocked by notes/analytic_results.md:75-80 and notes/periodfind_results.md (Theorem T).
8. Fixed-char quasi-polynomial DL refinements (Lido / Kleinjung-Wesolowski follow-ups, 2024–2025) & miscellaneous arXiv claims (Murru et al. arXiv:2409.03486 at L[1/2]; Friedlander arXiv:2504.21168 at O(sqrt(N))): Fixed-char Frobenius x^q - x has no carry-free lift to Z/N (exhibiting additive Frobenius mod N already factors N). Blocked by notes/smoothbuild_results.md:521-525 (systeq Prop F) and notes/heurnfs_results.md:450-459.

---

### 4. Final Ranking of Surviving Mechanisms

1. M1 — Type-D Relative-Rank m >= 3 Non-Power Linked Module (grdeg Door (i)): P(alpha < 1/3, heuristic) = 0.4%.
   - Falsification test: LLL-construct non-monic degree-n (n = 3, 4, 5) linked extensions over Z[i] with non-power relative-rank-3 generators; falsified if min_{genuine, A_2!=0} log|F|/log N scales as 4/(2n - 1) (confirming relative R1) rather than 2/(2n).
2. M2 — Class-Group Positive-Definite 2D-CRT Capacity Constructor (CG-2D-CRT): P(alpha < 1/3, heuristic) = 0.2%.
   - Falsification test: Test algebraic/polynomial-ideal CRT list-decoding on Q_m(k, v) mod q^(e_q) along the beta = 1/4 path for 48-96-bit N; falsified if runtime to beat random-walk hitting scales as K^(Omega(1)) rather than pi(B)^(O(1)).
3. M3 — Non-Exact Evaluated Multi-Presentation Split Pencils (nonexact O1/O2): P(alpha < 1/3, heuristic) = 0.1%.
   - Falsification test: Gröbner/resultant search for degree-M split polynomials P_A across 2-presentation mod-N pencils F_0 + nu*F_1 at 32-48 bits; falsified if cost per |P_A(m) mod* N| <= B^2 hit matches (N/B^2) random trials.
